TASK: four comments claim more than their code guarantees. Change comment text only, never code. Read the code each comment describes before rewording it.

1. `.github/workflows/trigger-index-rebuild.yml`, the comment above `concurrency:`, ends: "leaves the index unrebuilt until the next push to the branch". A push made with the default GITHUB_TOKEN also starts no run, so the true statement is: until a later push that starts a workflow run. Match `.github/workflows/README.md`'s row for this workflow, which says "until a later push that does start one".
2. `.skilled/hooks/task-dispatch/lib/dispatch-guard.cjs`, the comment on the loop-state lock's temp-file sweep says a temp file's age proves it is not in flight. Age only makes it eligible for removal: a creator paused longer than that age loses its temp file and then skips its update. Say that.
3. Same file, the break-lock comment says a break lock is never moved out from under a contender. That holds except when the breaker holding it has died, in which case another process retires it. State the exception.
4. `.skilled/hooks/post-edit-quality/lib/post-edit-router.cjs`, the comment block above `BEARER_SCHEME_WORD` / `BEARER_TOKEN_SHAPE` describes which Bearer tokens are redacted but omits the two thresholds the patterns enforce: the token run must be at least 8 characters, and a run with no digit or symbol counts as a token only when it is at least 16 characters and contains an uppercase letter. Read the regexes and state the thresholds they actually enforce.

Code standards: match the surrounding comment style and density. A comment states the durable WHY only. Never put finding ids, task ids, spec paths, phase numbers or packet numbers in a comment.

